  "notes": "Source: official BCCC Catalog 2024-2025 (catoid=12), 'Program: Dental Hygiene, AAS' — Prerequisites + Suggested Sequence of Courses transcribed verbatim. Selective admission: 2.5 cumulative GPA, ACCUPLACER, mandatory info session, TEAS (2 attempt limit), Biology Placement Exam (test out of BIO 101), computer literacy requirement; ~20 seats ranked by points. The two 0-credit admission requirements (Biology Placement Exam, Computer Literacy Exam) are documented here, not as courses. Prereqs must be completed prior to the Spring Semester for Fall Pre-Clinical admission (Total Prerequisite Credits 14). CREDIT DISCREPANCY: the catalog prints 'Program Total 70' but the sequenced credits sum to 68 (prereqs 14 + semesters 16/11/15/12); recorded as sequenced (68) per the iron rule of never inventing credits. All courses in the program sequence must be completed with a grade of C or higher. Program accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA); graduates are eligible for the National Board Examination and the ADEX Dental Hygiene Examination. Per-course prerequisites are not published on the program page; prereq lists are empty. [Coordinator correction 2026-10-01: total_credits set to 54 (= sum of sequenced course credits) per corpus convention (external_prereqs excluded from the sum; cf. ABAC plans); collector had recorded 68 including the prerequisite phase. The catalog's printed program total and the prerequisite phase remain documented above.]",
